      "writtenOn": "2022-10-26T14:02:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e If the requester is killed while we are configuring the cgroup for the crosvm process, the crosvm process will be killed \n\nThat takes a few seconds (and only happens if nobody else is using VS), so I\u0027m not sure it\u0027s a mitigation.\n\n\u003e Perhaps it\u0027s better to kill the feature\n\nDaemonize mode is used in a bunch of our tests (and also is very useful for manually starting a VM and leaving it running to do some exploring with adb), so I\u0027d rather we didn\u0027t kill it.",
      "parentUuid": "a88d72d2_e4239499",
